o.stream`** — decided, not left open. An undecided coexistence of both\n+namespaces is a defect of the migration, not a steady state.\n+\n+This is recorded here because the plan that carried it,\n+`dao.stream.implementation-plan.md`, was consumed when its phases\n+completed; the decision it left open outlived it, and a transient plan is\n+safe to delete only once nothing in it is still owed.\n+\n+The remaining v1 consumers, each migrating under its own plan: `dao.space`\n+(index, query, schema, transactor), `dao.jing`'s remote adapter and DHT node,\n+`yin.io`'s file transports with `dao.gui.event` and\n+`dao.postgraphics.terminal`, `dao.runtime` (gated on the v1 VM's deletion),\n+`agent.tools`, and the demo and server surfaces. The v1 VM lineage is deleted\n+rather than migrated, under `yin.vm-consumers.implementation-plan.md`,\n+because a v2 twin already exists for every one of its consumers.\ndiff --git a/test/dao/space/stigmergy_test.clj b/test/dao/space/stigmergy_test.clj\nindex 634eda7..e78726c 100644\n--- a/test/dao/space/stigmergy_test.clj\n+++ b/test/dao/space/stigmergy_test.clj\n@@ -369,29 +369,35 @@\n         {before :e} (put-entity! agent {:marker/id \"pre-index\"})\n         addr-a (first (publish-and-materialize! [agent]))]\n     (testing \"a published manifest is an immutable snapshot of its stream\"\n-      (is (= #{[before \"pre-index\"]}\n-             (qv '[:find ?e ?id :where [?e :marker/id ?id]]\n-                 (query/current (index/published-index {:dao.jing/type\n-                                                        :dao.jing/file,\n-                                                        :path space-path}\n-                                                       addr-a))))))\n+      (let [opened (query/open-published!\n+                     (index/published-index {:dao.jing/type :dao.jing/file,\n+                                             :path space-path}\n+                                            addr-a))]\n+        (try (is (= #{[